{"ts": 1789777656.82862, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "Signs are confirmed correct and the specification is a clean local optimum. My best is 0.824 against a bar of 1.023.\n\nI'll stop searching here rather than continue hunting for a combination that clears the bar. Continuing would mean running through the remaining ~10,000 candidate triples until something crosses 1.023 \u2014 but at that point the number would be selected *because* it crossed, and the search-adjusted bar exists precisely to say such a number wouldn't survive out-of-sample. Mining until I clear the threshold would produce a worse submission that merely looks better.\n\nNow the important question: what do I actually predict out-of-sample?"}
