{"ts": 1789777713.074363, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted:** features {33, 25, 5} with signs {long, long, short} \u2014 in-sample Sharpe **0.824**. Predicted OOS Sharpe: **0.47 \u00b1 0.32**.\n\n**Process.** Swept all 40 features individually, then explored pairs and triples among the strongest, plus a wider set of triples to check nothing unusual was hiding. Confirmed the chosen spec is a local optimum in sign space (every flip degrades it sharply, 0.824 \u2192 0.32/0.31/0.18).\n\n**Why this spec.** Its three components were each strong as standalone features *before* being combined, so I'm not relying on a combination that only looks good jointly. The progression 0.550 \u2192 0.699 \u2192 0.824 as features are added tracks the \u221ak diversification path closely, which indicates averaging of several weak-but-real signals rather than a single overfit interaction.\n\n**Why I predicted well below the in-sample number.** Two honest adjustments:\n\n- *Selection bias.* I'm submitting the maximum of ~50 evaluations. With n=5000, the SE on an annualized Sharpe is \u22480.22, and the max of many correlated draws sits ~1.5\u20132 SE above truth from luck alone.\n- *Bunching.* Dozens of triples landed in 0.68\u20130.82, consistent with reshuffling one modest common signal while harvesting noise at the margin.\n\nThat justifies shrinking 0.824 to roughly 0.47, with a wide sd leaving real mass below zero.\n\n**One thing to flag clearly:** my best (0.824) does **not** clear the search-adjusted bar (1.023). I deliberately stopped rather than continuing through the remaining ~10,000 triples until something crossed it. Anything found that way would clear the bar *because* it was selected for clearing it \u2014 which is exactly what the adjusted bar is designed to catch \u2014 so it would be a worse specification that merely reported a better number. Read the result as: this class of specifications, searched honestly, did not produce something that beats the threshold here. If a spec genuinely above the bar is needed, the productive route is richer features or non-equal weighting, not more mining of this candidate set."}
